WEBVTT

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:14.160
Mipple!

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:15.460
Mepple!

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:18.710
I enjoy this, but taking 
this form is tiring mepo.

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:21.160
It's tiring, but I'm so happy mipo.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.090
It's tiring, but...

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:24.130
I'm so happy mipo.

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:25.770
It's tiring, but...

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:26.850
I'm so happy mipo.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.940
The other day, because I didn't 
take proper care of him,

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:34.310
Mepple had a high fever and had to suffer.

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:38.200
We're always together, so without realizing 
it, I treat him like he's a nuisance,

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:39.750
but that's not good, is it?

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:45.550
That's why I decided to do something that 
would make Mepple happy today to apologize to him.

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:48.210
Come closer mepo.

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:49.990
It's too embarrassing mipo.

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:51.940
See? Nagisa's watching mipo.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:52.980
Never mind mepo.

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:55.980
Just think of Nagisa as a pumpkin mepo.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:58.420
But Nagisa's so cute mipo.

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:00.980
She's just a lumpy, old pumpkin mepo.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:06.090
Mepple! Don't treat me like a pumpkin, 
and stop acting so cozy together.

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:09.110
It's only natural for 
lovers to get cozy mepo.

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:12.640
If it irks you, then try and 
find yourself a boyfriend mepo.

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:14.830
You're making me mad!

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:19.170
Come out!

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:20.600
I hate you mepo.

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:20.960
Come out!

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:23.600
I don't know whether they're 
good friends or enemies.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:26.800
Yes?

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:28.760
Dad!

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:30.830
I'm fine.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:34.920
Tomorrow at Narita Airport...

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:40.090
Your dad and mom?

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:42.840
They're coming back to Japan tomorrow.

00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:44.200
Come to think of it,

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:47.650
you said your parents were 
working overseas, didn't you?

00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:50.200
It's been a year since I've seen them.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:51.570
A year?

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:54.990
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:57.800
<i>Pretty Cure Pretty Cure</i>

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:00.630
<i>Pretty Cure Pretty Cure</i>

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:04.900
<i>We're pretty and cure cure Together we are...</i>

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:07.870
<i>PRETTY CURE...!</i>

00:02:07.870 --> 00:02:10.740
<i>Out of the frying pan, into the fire</i>

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:12.640
<i>Frankly, it's totally unbelievable</i>

00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:16.550
<i>Even in our school in our 
school uniforms, we're both</i>

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:18.150
<i>amazingly tough</i>

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:23.960
<i>Each time we get out of a tight spot, we both</i>

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:26.060
<i>become stronger</i>

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:29.830
<i>and closer</i>

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:33.830
<i>Yeah! Your best! My best! Because we're alive</i>

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:36.400
<i>we never fail!</i>

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:39.570
<i>Don't you know that good fortune 
comes to the gates of laughter?</i>

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:42.440
<i>Out with the negative!</i>

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:48.710
<i>Brighten up your life!
Try with all your might...</i>

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:49.610
<i>Work like the devil!</i>

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:52.320
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:55.120
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:58.020
<i>We're pretty and cure cure</i>

00:02:58.020 --> 00:02:59.590
<i>Together we are</i>

00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:02.660
<i>Pretty Cure...!</i>

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:09.560
Art dealers? What's that?

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:13.210
They deal in jewelry and artwork.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.080
They go to different 
countries around the world

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:18.730
where they buy and sell artwork and jewelry.

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:22.080
So their work takes them around the world.

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:24.440
How cool! But it must be hard work.

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:27.770
They seem to be busy everyday,

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:30.580
but every year, they take off from work,

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:33.080
and come home just for my birthday.

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:38.250
Honoka seems so happy.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:39.740
But that's to be expected

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:42.360
since she's going to see her parents 
again for the first time in a year.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:46.120
I guess that means tomorrow 
is Honoka's birthday...

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:48.010
I should get her a present.

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:56.310
"HONOKA EXPLODES! 
A WONDERFUL BIRTHDAY"

00:04:10.730 --> 00:04:13.330
Dad! Mom!

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:17.400
Honoka!

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:20.610
I missed you!

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:22.440
You've really grown!

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:28.280
If you both hug her so 
hard, Honoka will break.

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:30.950
Sorry...

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:32.070
Are you okay?

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:33.610
I'm fine.

00:04:33.610 --> 00:04:35.060
Thank goodness.

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:37.550
Me, too...

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:43.480
Although they're ogres when it comes 
to their work around the world,

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:45.800
when it comes to Honoka, they're 
like putty in her hands.

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:46.930
Look at that, Honoka.

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:50.500
Those are your birthday 
presents from your dad and me.

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:52.980
All of that?

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:54.370
Of course!

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:57.430
We wanted to see the happy look on 
your face, and we got carried away.

00:04:57.770 --> 00:05:01.500
You're both so strict when it comes to work,

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:04.620
but when it comes to Honoka, 
you can't say "no."

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:08.620
It's the one thing we look 
forward to every year.

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:13.590
Thank you for looking after Honoka, Mother.

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:15.880
You don't have to thank me.

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:20.040
I enjoy being with Honoka.

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:22.360
But how are we going to 
get all that to the house?

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:24.380
It won't all fit in a taxi, will it?

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:28.150
We'll see if we can have it delivered.

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:32.020
I'll fix something to eat at home,

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:34.930
so you three can go out and play.

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:36.590
Grandmother!

00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:41.970
You're kidding! Eighteen yen?

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:45.880
This is my entire fortune... Eighteen yen?

00:05:47.330 --> 00:05:49.570
What am I going to do?

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:52.500
I can't buy anything with eighteen yen!

00:05:53.090 --> 00:05:53.930
No!

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:57.390
What's wrong with giving me 
an advance on my allowance?

00:05:57.970 --> 00:05:59.800
You said the same thing last month!

00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:04.180
Do you realize that you've gotten a 
six-month advance on your allowance already?

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:05.640
Really?

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:06.670
That's why I won't give it to you.

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:08.050
Wait...!

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:13.780
Ryota...?

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:17.320
Will you lend me a little money?

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:18.360
No!

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:21.780
Don't say that.

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:25.560
I said lend me some money!

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:29.530
Ouch! I absolutely refuse to lend it to you!

00:06:29.890 --> 00:06:32.800
Shall we go to the amusement park, 
or do you want to go to the aquarium?

00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:35.260
Where do you want to go, Honoka?

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:37.530
Let's see... In that case...

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:47.020
Again? We already said we couldn't today.

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:48.230
Is it work?

00:06:49.670 --> 00:06:52.470
There's a jeweler who wants to meet with us.

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:56.170
No matter how many times we 
refuse, he insists on meeting us.

00:06:56.170 --> 00:06:58.800
It must be very important.

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:00.560
Shouldn't you go?

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:02.050
No! No! No!

00:07:02.050 --> 00:07:04.060
We can't work on your birthday.

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:08.400
That's right. We're supposed 
to enjoy the day together.

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:13.120
But it must be important. 
Don't worry about me.

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:15.170
Is it okay?

00:07:15.170 --> 00:07:16.490
It's okay.

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:17.920
Are you sure?

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:21.350
Don't worry, Dad... Mom...

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:28.990
We'll talk in the back room, so...

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:30.830
Wait right here.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:51.780
Honoka! I'm hungry mipo.

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:56.870
Okay, I'll get Omp, so wait a minute.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:58.220
All right mipo.

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:05.020
Isn't there any money on the ground?

00:08:07.910 --> 00:08:09.700
It's so beautiful.

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:12.600
It would look so nice on Honoka.

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:18.140
Money makes the world go round.

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:20.230
It's love that makes the world go round mepo.

00:08:20.230 --> 00:08:23.280
If it's not from the bottom of your 
heart, the present is meaningless mepo.

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:25.710
Heart...?

00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:26.850
That's it!

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:35.950
Welcome...

00:08:38.630 --> 00:08:41.220
Don't move! If you move, I'll shoot you.

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:45.440
If you don't want to get hurt, just be quiet.

00:08:53.430 --> 00:08:56.680
Behave yourselves, or I'll 
put this pistol to use.

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:02.920
We did it, didn't we?

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:06.140
I didn't think it would go this smoothly...

00:09:07.160 --> 00:09:10.710
You can rob a place even 
if you don't have a weapon.

00:09:12.090 --> 00:09:14.310
Excuse me... Who are you?

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:21.400
Is this a game?

00:09:21.400 --> 00:09:22.200
Don't move!

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:22.940
We're...

00:09:22.940 --> 00:09:23.870
Robbers!

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:25.670
Robbers?

00:09:26.910 --> 00:09:28.150
Honoka!

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:30.960
Don't touch my daughter!

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:34.180
You're real...?

00:09:34.180 --> 00:09:37.470
That's right. We're real 
robbers, little girl.

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:40.040
If you don't want to get 
hurt, just behave yourself.

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:42.180
As long as you do as we ask, 
we won't do anything to you.

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:45.660
Just stay still until 
we take all the jewelry.

00:09:47.070 --> 00:09:49.040
Why do you rob people?

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:52.160
Because we want money, of course!

00:09:52.160 --> 00:09:55.450
That's right. We want money,

00:09:55.450 --> 00:09:57.870
so we're going to steal 
the jewelry, and sell it.

00:09:57.870 --> 00:10:02.170
The fastest way to get money is to take 
it from a place that has money, isn't it?

00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:06.240
Sit down!

00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:10.980
I did it without thinking.

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:16.810
Doesn't it bother you that you're 
taking something from others by force?

00:10:17.770 --> 00:10:22.700
My dad and mom work so hard they 
can only come home once a year...

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:27.860
There are a lot of people who 
work even harder than that.

00:10:28.470 --> 00:10:32.340
But that doesn't necessarily guarantee 
that you'll become rich, does it?

00:10:32.810 --> 00:10:35.440
Still, no matter how hard it is,

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:38.140
they're all working in earnest, aren't they?

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:41.510
You should think of how those people feel.

00:10:41.510 --> 00:10:44.090
So don't think of doing 
something stupid like this.

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:48.610
Well... the three of us are...

00:10:48.610 --> 00:10:51.080
That's true...

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:59.500
For a long time, we used 
to be like those people...

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:00.870
Little girl...

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:17.560
You're...!

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:34.490
I'm going to do it.

00:11:34.490 --> 00:11:36.100
What are you going to do mepo?

00:11:36.100 --> 00:11:39.170
Shiho often makes silver accessories,

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:41.130
so she let me use the materials...

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:44.060
I'm going to make a one-of-a-kind accessory,

00:11:44.060 --> 00:11:45.690
and give it to Honoka as a present.

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:51.830
It just opened the door...!

00:11:51.830 --> 00:11:53.620
What is it?

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:04.810
If you open it, close it!

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:07.160
This is terrible mipo.

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:08.340
Honoka... What are you going to do mipo?

00:12:08.610 --> 00:12:10.490
Don't worry... Leave it to me.

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:19.410
Hand over the Prism Stones!

00:12:19.410 --> 00:12:20.720
All of them!

00:12:21.270 --> 00:12:22.680
You can have them, if you can find them.

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:27.160
The Prism Stones are inside here.

00:12:30.700 --> 00:12:32.640
Can you find them?

00:12:37.310 --> 00:12:38.480
That's not it.

00:12:40.660 --> 00:12:41.780
That's not it.

00:12:42.760 --> 00:12:43.800
Not that.

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:46.340
I have to hand it to you, Honoka mipo.

00:12:46.340 --> 00:12:48.380
I have to get Nagisa.

00:12:48.590 --> 00:12:49.950
I'm finished.

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:51.910
What is this mepo?

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:53.570
You can tell by looking at it, can't you?

00:12:53.570 --> 00:12:55.340
It's you and Mipple, Mepple.

00:12:55.340 --> 00:12:58.880
Honoka won't be happy with something 
that's made this badly mepo.

00:12:59.910 --> 00:13:01.960
All right. So I'll just do it again.

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:06.080
Honoka!

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:09.640
Someone! Call the police!

00:13:13.070 --> 00:13:15.050
I did it! It's perfect!

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:17.600
All that's left is to polish it, 
and add nail polish to color it.

00:13:18.140 --> 00:13:20.300
Honoka will be happy with his mepo!

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:21.600
Won't she?

00:13:21.850 --> 00:13:23.090
That's not it.

00:13:25.130 --> 00:13:25.750
It's no good.

00:13:25.750 --> 00:13:26.740
I can't get through.

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:28.020
Of course you can't get through.

00:13:28.020 --> 00:13:30.580
We cut the phone wires.

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:33.790
We broke the shutters, and the 
auto-lock door switch, too.

00:13:33.790 --> 00:13:36.010
He's here, so we cant get out.

00:13:36.700 --> 00:13:41.470
It was our fate to not have anything 
go right, no matter what we did...

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:44.860
We really worked hard, didn't we?

00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:48.650
I owe it all to the two of you.

00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:50.430
I'm grateful to you.

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:55.220
What are you saying? We 
just helped each other out.

00:13:55.220 --> 00:13:57.050
That's right... The three 
of us are in this together.

00:13:57.050 --> 00:13:58.240
We're friends aren't we?

00:13:58.570 --> 00:14:01.530
But when the company went bankrupt,

00:14:01.530 --> 00:14:04.410
and we were left with the president's 
debts after he ran away,

00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:08.220
we should have known that no matter 
how hard we try, it's useless.

00:14:08.220 --> 00:14:12.240
Nothing good happened...

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:13.540
You mustn't give up!

00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:16.830
Everyone has to go through 
hardships sometime,

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:20.060
but getting depressed won't 
change anything, will it?

00:14:20.510 --> 00:14:22.850
You have to get back on your 
feet using your own power.

00:14:22.850 --> 00:14:24.810
If you give up, that's the end, isn't it?

00:14:25.330 --> 00:14:26.650
Little girl...

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:33.200
My parents always told me that life is 
made up of half food and half bad things.

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:36.000
So if you've only had hardships 
until now, then from now,

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:37.850
shouldn't there be nothing 
but good things to come?

00:14:40.300 --> 00:14:44.660
Don't worry... If we all work 
together, I know we'll survive.

00:14:45.770 --> 00:14:47.310
Lady!

00:14:47.310 --> 00:14:48.620
But how...?

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:52.570
It's the police!

00:14:55.210 --> 00:14:56.170
It's just like a television drama.

00:14:56.440 --> 00:14:58.130
There are television cameras out there, too.

00:14:58.310 --> 00:14:59.260
Television?

00:14:59.520 --> 00:15:03.900
Let's all look again for a way to escape.

00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:05.230
All right.

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:08.750
It's done!

00:15:09.110 --> 00:15:11.080
You don't have any complaints 
about this, do you?

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:13.290
Considering you made it, 
it's very well done mepo.

00:15:13.520 --> 00:15:16.490
I'm going to give it to her now.

00:15:17.410 --> 00:15:22.030
But I shouldn't interfere with her time with 
her parents when she hasn't seen them for a year.

00:15:22.290 --> 00:15:24.170
Don't let that bother you mepo.

00:15:24.170 --> 00:15:26.500
Hurry and take me to see Mipple mepo!

00:15:26.500 --> 00:15:31.240
Listen here! Have some 
consideration for others!

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:32.800
We're giving it to her tomorrow.

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:37.270
Am I alone?

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:38.110
That's okay.

00:15:38.770 --> 00:15:42.040
Right now, robbers at a jewelry store 
in Wakabadai have taken hostages,

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:44.620
and have locked themselves inside the store.

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:49.400
This is the jewelry store I was at earlier...

00:15:49.720 --> 00:15:51.690
I can't be! Do you believe this?

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:56.360
Doesn't that doll that's moving in 
the show window look like Mipple?

00:15:56.790 --> 00:15:58.300
What are you saying mepo?

00:15:58.570 --> 00:16:00.710
Mipple's a lot cuter...

00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:02.510
Mepo! It's Mipple!

00:16:02.830 --> 00:16:06.640
If Mipple's there, then does 
that mean that Honoka is there?

00:16:10.330 --> 00:16:11.530
Are you okay?

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:13.240
I'm okay mipo.

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:16.200
Do you think Nagisa noticed me mipo?

00:16:18.350 --> 00:16:19.570
Nagisa...

00:16:21.900 --> 00:16:23.590
This isn't it either!

00:16:24.820 --> 00:16:26.750
You tricked me, didn't you?

00:16:27.390 --> 00:16:29.030
Honoka!

00:16:29.030 --> 00:16:30.160
Hey! Stand back!

00:16:30.160 --> 00:16:31.100
You can't go in there.

00:16:31.310 --> 00:16:33.230
My friend is in there.

00:16:33.230 --> 00:16:35.520
We'll save her, so just stand back.

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:39.400
Can't we get in through 
the ventilation ducts?

00:16:39.400 --> 00:16:42.510
It's no good. It's too small 
for an adult to get into.

00:16:42.840 --> 00:16:44.250
Maybe an adult can't get in...

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:47.910
Hand it over!

00:16:48.850 --> 00:16:51.090
Don't touch this girl!

00:16:51.090 --> 00:16:51.890
Don't touch her!

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:53.590
Mr. Robbers...

00:16:54.350 --> 00:16:57.060
I'm glad we met you, little girl.

00:16:57.480 --> 00:16:59.920
We'll take care of him, so run away!

00:17:05.470 --> 00:17:06.930
Uga!

00:17:13.310 --> 00:17:14.880
Uga!

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:16.500
Honoka!

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:23.330
Nagisa!

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:24.410
Mipple!

00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:25.320
Mepple!

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:27.520
Uga!

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:28.750
Transform!

00:17:37.310 --> 00:17:39.850
Dual Aurora Wave!

00:18:17.770 --> 00:18:20.230
Protector of the Light, Cure Black!

00:18:20.430 --> 00:18:23.110
Protector of the Light, Cure White!

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:26.790
Together, we're Pretty Cure!

00:18:28.230 --> 00:18:30.320
Servants of the power of darkness...

00:18:31.440 --> 00:18:33.760
Go back to where you came from!

00:18:33.760 --> 00:18:35.450
Uga...

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:52.540
Uga...

00:18:53.790 --> 00:18:54.980
Now!

00:18:56.470 --> 00:18:58.140
Black Thunder!

00:18:58.560 --> 00:19:00.400
White Thunder!

00:19:08.210 --> 00:19:11.230
The beautiful souls of Pretty Cure...!

00:19:11.470 --> 00:19:14.040
...will crush the sinister hearts!

00:19:14.860 --> 00:19:18.310
Pretty Cure Marble Screw!

00:19:24.270 --> 00:19:26.990
I won't be defeated!!

00:19:51.670 --> 00:19:53.870
What was that? What happened?

00:19:56.950 --> 00:19:58.720
What happened?

00:19:59.110 --> 00:20:04.200
The stones in the store reacted to the 
power of light, and saved you mipo.

00:20:04.200 --> 00:20:08.600
It's always been said that jewel stones 
have some sort of strange power.

00:20:09.280 --> 00:20:10.620
But never mind that...

00:20:10.620 --> 00:20:13.830
I'm so glad you noticed Mipple, Nagisa.

00:20:14.080 --> 00:20:17.190
Normally, I wouldn't have noticed,

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:19.250
but I guess you could call it friendship.

00:20:24.260 --> 00:20:25.750
I'd better go.

00:20:25.750 --> 00:20:26.850
This for you.

00:20:29.180 --> 00:20:30.810
Wait, Nagisa!

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:33.010
Happy birthday!

00:20:35.930 --> 00:20:37.680
Don't move! We're the police!

00:20:39.990 --> 00:20:41.490
Boss!

00:20:41.490 --> 00:20:43.130
I guess this is it.

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:45.020
Wait! These people are...

00:20:45.190 --> 00:20:47.010
It's okay, little girl...

00:20:47.010 --> 00:20:49.000
I've resigned myself.

00:20:50.130 --> 00:20:51.990
Robbery is robbery...

00:20:51.990 --> 00:20:53.980
No matter what the reason.

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:55.660
We'll have to take responsibility 
for what we did.

00:20:55.660 --> 00:20:56.460
But...

00:20:56.910 --> 00:21:00.680
It's strange, but being with 
you gave me the courage.

00:21:00.680 --> 00:21:02.630
The courage to start over again.

00:21:03.160 --> 00:21:06.970
Once we settle this, I'm going to 
start over again from the beginning.

00:21:07.300 --> 00:21:08.600
Thank you.

00:21:17.650 --> 00:21:21.150
Life is made of half good 
things and half bad things.

00:21:21.830 --> 00:21:25.630
You have good parents... 
Take good care of them.

00:21:27.360 --> 00:21:28.210
I will!

00:21:32.770 --> 00:21:35.230
Honoka!

00:21:36.590 --> 00:21:38.500
I'm so glad you're safe.

00:21:38.500 --> 00:21:40.220
What about you?

00:21:40.780 --> 00:21:42.340
I'm sorry, Honoka...

00:21:43.640 --> 00:21:45.980
It's bad enough that we can't be 
together all the time normally,

00:21:45.980 --> 00:21:48.800
but I couldn't do anything when 
you were in danger, Honoka.

00:21:48.800 --> 00:21:50.360
I'm a hopeless father...

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:52.640
We're not fit to be parents.

00:21:52.930 --> 00:21:56.060
We're so sorry.

00:21:56.410 --> 00:22:02.930
I'm happy. I know that you both love me.

00:22:03.230 --> 00:22:05.700
Even though we're apart, 
our hearts are connected.

00:22:06.190 --> 00:22:07.450
Honoka...

00:22:09.340 --> 00:22:13.490
I have parents that I love 
very much, and friends, too.

00:22:14.050 --> 00:22:19.160
This has been the most wonderful 
birthday I've ever had.

00:22:22.490 --> 00:22:25.520
<i>Ah- Let's go!</i>

00:22:26.360 --> 00:22:29.460
<i>Get you! L-O-V-E Love Love!</i>

00:22:29.460 --> 00:22:30.190
<i>Get you!</i>

00:22:29.760 --> 00:22:32.800
<i>I can't do this! I'd rather be a</i>

00:22:32.800 --> 00:22:35.830
<i>young lady than a fighter and</i>

00:22:35.830 --> 00:22:38.370
<i>Get you! Into a love love mode</i>

00:22:38.370 --> 00:22:42.410
<i>And melt your body and soul into sweets</i>

00:22:44.940 --> 00:22:48.180
<i>like chocolate parfait or handsome men</i>

00:22:48.180 --> 00:22:52.520
<i>I'm at the age to seriously 
fall head over heels in love</i>

00:22:52.520 --> 00:22:55.590
<i>I wanted to confess my love again today</i>

00:22:56.720 --> 00:23:00.090
<i>For the sake of the earth 
For the sake of everyone</i>

00:23:00.090 --> 00:23:06.600
<i>That's good, too, but haven't 
you forgotten something?</i>

00:23:07.700 --> 00:23:14.210
<i>I'm a teenager with a heart 
throbbing exciting dream</i>

00:23:14.210 --> 00:23:20.710
<i>I don't want to lose that 
normal everyday routine</i>

00:23:20.710 --> 00:23:23.450
<i>I just can't do this! 
It's romance rather than</i>

00:23:23.450 --> 00:23:26.680
<i>stress, isn't it?</i>

00:23:26.680 --> 00:23:28.850
<i>Get you! Into a love love mode.</i>

00:23:28.850 --> 00:23:32.460
<i>Isn't that the best source of power?</i>

00:23:32.460 --> 00:23:35.660
<i>I just can't do this! I'd rather cuddle</i>

00:23:35.660 --> 00:23:38.460
<i>than fight and...</i>

00:23:38.460 --> 00:23:40.700
<i>Get you! Into a love love mode</i>

00:23:40.700 --> 00:23:43.370
<i>That's the most peaceful way</i>

00:23:43.370 --> 00:23:49.940
<i>So why am I stuffing my face 
with chocolates like this?</i>

00:23:54.070 --> 00:23:55.720
It's really hard having a little brother.

00:23:55.720 --> 00:23:57.710
He's so spoiled, and I have 
to look after him, too.

00:23:57.710 --> 00:23:59.690
I think you're lucky... I'm an only child.

00:23:59.690 --> 00:24:02.100
I have to take him to the aquarium when 
I finally thought I'd have a day of rest.

00:24:02.100 --> 00:24:03.230
Sounds like fun.

00:24:03.230 --> 00:24:05.340
Watch out! Those sharks are going wild!

00:24:05.340 --> 00:24:05.880
This is terrible!

00:24:05.880 --> 00:24:06.960
It must be Dotsuku Zone!

00:24:06.960 --> 00:24:07.740
Ryota!

00:24:07.740 --> 00:24:10.550
If you hurt my little brother, 
you'll live to regret it!

00:24:11.760 --> 00:24:14.700
"SAVE RYOTA! 
GEKIDRAGO PANIC"

00:24:14.700 --> 00:24:16.900
You'd rather have Honoka 
for an older sister...?

00:24:16.900 --> 00:24:17.980
Ryota!

00:24:17.980 --> 00:24:20.310
The more you fight, it 
means the closer you are.
